      en: "Vjeternik Ridge in Durmitor National Park extends about 8 km, reaching up to 2,300 m. Composed of limestone, it features sharp arêtes and deep gorges. The ridge is popular with climbers, offering challenging routes. Wind speeds on the ridge can exceed 100 km/h. Vegetation is predominantly alpine meadows and lichens. The ridge provides impressive views of the Tara River canyon. The area is also known for its diverse birdlife, including the peregrine falcon.",
